# MedFinderAdmin Cursor Rules

## Stack
Angular 18 standalone components, Angular Material, AngularFire, Firebase. TypeScript strict mode.

## Firebase Access
- All Firebase calls must go through a service in `src/app/services/` — never in a component
- Follow the naming pattern `*-data-access.service.ts` for new data services
- Privileged Auth operations (create/update/delete Firebase Auth users) must go in Cloud Functions, not the client

## Components
- All components are standalone — use `imports: []` in the decorator, no NgModules
- Create/edit UI always uses Angular Material MatDialog with a dedicated `edit-*-dialog` component
- Wrap async operations with `LoadingService.show()` / `LoadingService.hide()`

## TypeScript
- Strict mode is on — no implicit `any`, always type parameters and return values
- Use interfaces from `src/app/models/` for all Firebase data shapes

## Sensitive Files
- `src/environments/firebase-config.ts` is gitignored — never suggest committing it
- Reference `firebase-config.template.ts` for the expected object shape
